userStories.description:
**Goal** — Provide an uncatalogued general AgentResource and its canonical prompt for model-only chat dispatch.

**Motivation** — Asked to "dispatch native openai-codex/gpt-6-luna", the chat agent had to guess a carrier agent: it called `agent: "explore"` (refused as unknown) and then `agent: "Explore"`.

**Approach** — A new module `packages/nax/src/chat/builtin-agent.ts` exports:

```typescript
export const GENERAL_AGENT_NAME = "general";
export const GENERAL_AGENT_DESCRIPTION = "Runs a self-contained task on the model you pass";
/** The agent a nax-agents__run call with a model and no agent runs on. */
export function generalAgent(): AgentResource;
```

`generalAgent()` returns `{ kind: "agent", name: GENERAL_AGENT_NAME, qualifiedName: GENERAL_AGENT_NAME, description: GENERAL_AGENT_DESCRIPTION, prompt: buildGeneralAgentPrompt(), path: "", origin: { kind: "nax-builtin" } }` with no `model` and no `tools` keys. With no `tools`, `mapSubagentTools` returns no `allowedTools`, so a native run admits every parent tool and an ACP run gets the chat profile (the existing rules for an agent without `tools:`). `GENERAL_AGENT_NAME` and `generalAgent` are exported from the `@/chat` barrel.

`ResourceOrigin` (`packages/nax/src/resources/types.ts`) gains `{ readonly kind: "nax-builtin" }`. `originLabel` (`packages/nax/src/resources/listing.ts`) becomes an exported function (not added to the `@/resources` barrel) and returns `"built-in"` for it. The general agent is never added to a `ResourceCatalog`: `/agents`, the agents index and `findAgent` do not see it.

`buildGeneralAgentPrompt()` is a new function in `packages/nax/src/prompts/builders/agents-builder.ts`, exported from `@/prompts`, returning exactly:

```text
You are a general-purpose subagent. Complete the task you are given with the tools you have, then reply with a concise final answer: the agent that called you reads only your last message.
```

**Scope** — In: the new resource factory, origin union/label, prompt builder, named barrel exports and builtin-agent.test.ts. Out: provider validation/dispatch and instructions advertisement (US-002), provenance resolution/metadata (US-003), Agent-card rendering (US-004), ACP pending events (US-005), unread-tool correction (US-006). Do not add general to catalog discovery or change the CLI's required agent argument.

**Interface** —
```typescript
export const GENERAL_AGENT_NAME = "general";
export const GENERAL_AGENT_DESCRIPTION = "Runs a self-contained task on the model you pass";
/** The agent a nax-agents__run call with a model and no agent runs on. */
export function generalAgent(): AgentResource;
export function buildGeneralAgentPrompt(): string;
export function originLabel(origin: ResourceOrigin): string;
```

**Goal** — Identify undeclared names in unread tool_call text and append bounded nearest-declared-name suggestions without executing the text.

**Motivation** — `unreadToolCallFollowUp` (`packages/nax-agent/src/native/session/loop-handlers.ts`) lists every declared tool name but does not say which name in the block was wrong.

**Approach** — A new module `packages/nax-agent/src/native/session/unread-tool-call.ts` exports:

```typescript
export const MAX_SUGGEST_DISTANCE = 2;
/** Tool names written in the <tool_call> blocks of an assistant reply, first-seen order, no duplicates. */
export function writtenToolNames(content: string): string[];
/** The declared name nearest to `written`, case-insensitive, within MAX_SUGGEST_DISTANCE; first in declared order on a tie. */
export function nearestToolName(written: string, declared: readonly string[]): string | undefined;
export function buildUnreadToolCallFollowUp(content: string, declared: readonly string[]): string;
```

A tool name is a string matching `^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]{0,63}$` (`TOOL_NAME_PATTERN`). `writtenToolNames` scans each `<tool_call>` marker to the next `</tool_call>` (or the end of the text). Within a block, the name is the first `"name"` JSON string value (`"name"` followed by optional spaces, `:`, optional spaces and a double-quoted string), kept only when it matches `TOOL_NAME_PATTERN`. When the block has no `"name"` value, the name is the run of name characters that starts at the first non-whitespace character after the marker, kept only when that character is a letter or `_` and the run matches `TOOL_NAME_PATTERN`. A block yielding neither contributes no name.

`nearestToolName` compares lowercase forms with Levenshtein distance; it returns the declared name (in its declared casing) with the smallest distance when that distance is at most `MAX_SUGGEST_DISTANCE`, and undefined otherwise or when `declared` is empty.

`buildUnreadToolCallFollowUp` returns the existing text, then, for each written name that is not exactly a declared name, appends one space and `` `<written>` is not a declared tool; did you mean `<nearest>`? `` or, with no near match, `` `<written>` is not a declared tool. ``. The existing text is: `Your reply contains a <tool_call> block that was not run: it did not read as a call of a declared tool. Call tools through the tool interface, using one of these exact names: <names or (none)>.`

`unreadToolCallFollowUp` in `loop-handlers.ts` keeps its guards and its once-per-turn `sent` flag, and returns `{ followUp: buildUnreadToolCallFollowUp(last.content, toolNames()) }`.

This is a nax-agent string, not a nax prompt builder: the nax prompt-builder rule covers `packages/nax/src`, and the follow-up already lives in nax-agent.

**Scope** — In: new pure extraction/distance/text helpers, existing native handler delegation, helper tests and native handler/round-trip integration regressions. Out: general-agent/provider dispatch (US-001/US-002), model provenance/card display (US-003/US-004), ACP pending events (US-005). Raising the once-per-turn cap on the unread tool-call follow-up. Rewriting or running a misspelled text tool call automatically; the model must call the tool itself. US-006 only: reading the tool name from a top-level JSON key; the first `"name"` string value in the block is taken even when it is nested inside the arguments.

**Interface** —
```typescript
export const MAX_SUGGEST_DISTANCE = 2;
/** Tool names written in the <tool_call> blocks of an assistant reply, first-seen order, no duplicates. */
export function writtenToolNames(content: string): string[];
/** The declared name nearest to `written`, case-insensitive, within MAX_SUGGEST_DISTANCE; first in declared order on a tie. */
export function nearestToolName(written: string, declared: readonly string[]): string | undefined;
export function buildUnreadToolCallFollowUp(content: string, declared: readonly string[]): string;
```

**Implementation/test notes** — Create unread-tool-call.ts and test/unit/native/session/unread-tool-call-text.test.ts; these are module-level exports, not a request to expand the package public API. Keep handler registration order/plugin followUp precedence and setting sent before returning intact. In test/unit/native/session/unread-tool-call.test.ts, the existing BLOCK names ScrashpadWrite and the default tools are Read/Write, neither within distance 2; append one space followed by the exact sentence `` `ScrashpadWrite` is not a declared tool.``. Update the no-tools test to contain the existing (none) phrase and end with that same sentence; guard/once-per-turn tests stay. In test/integration/session/native-unread-tool-call.test.ts, replace the old declared-sentence toEndWith with contains plus the correct appended sentence for ScrashpadWrite against the actual declared names. Also trigger the before_turn_end registry seam with Read/ScratchpadWrite and confirm the suggestion reaches followUp once. Use exact string literals for text regressions rather than deriving every expected string from the function under test.
